      "side": 1,
      "message": ":) Although this upstream fix came in later and thus technically it\u0027s this upstream fix that introduced this race (by fixing another race), we know that the root cause is not in the upstream fix but in our naive way of reusing host driver\u0027s code without providing serialization guarantees expected by that code from an upper layer (which are provided by `iommu_group-\u003emutex` in the host driver\u0027s case).\n\nSo I\u0027d rather specify the original commit 3cf82cef8d7f (\"ANDROID: iommu/vt-d: pKVM: Legacy mode context update hypercalls\") (in particular, so that we know to squash it into that commit when rebasing to a newer kernel).",
